Q: Calculate KCV from 3DES key A: <p>Here is a Java example to calculate the KCV.</p>
<p>Note that the key you provided (DBFE96D0A5F09D24) is 8 bytes long (16 hex chars). While you mentioned &quot;3DES&quot;, an 8-byte key effectively functions as Single DES. The KCV is typically calculated by encrypting a block of nulls (00...00) with the key and taking the first few bytes of the result.</p>
<p>Here is the Java implementation using javax.crypto:</p>
<pre><code>import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;
import javax.xml.bind.DatatypeConverter; // Or use any Hex utility

public class KcvCalculator {

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        String keyHex = &quot;DBFE96D0A5F09D24&quot;;

        // Convert Hex String to Byte Array
        byte[] keyBytes =  DatatypeConverter.parseHexBinary(keyHex);

        // Determine algorithm based on key length (8 bytes = DES, 16/24 bytes = TripleDES)
        String algorithm = &quot;DES&quot;; 
        if (keyBytes.length == 16 || keyBytes.length == 24) {
            algorithm = &quot;DESede&quot;;
        }

        // Prepare the Cipher
        SecretKeySpec keySpec = new SecretKeySpec(keyBytes, algorithm);
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(algorithm + &quot;/ECB/NoPadding&quot;);
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, keySpec);

        // Encrypt 8 bytes of Zeros
        byte[] data = new byte[8]; // Default is all zeros
        byte[] result = cipher.doFinal(data);

        // Convert result to Hex
        String resultHex = DatatypeConverter.printHexBinary(result);

        // KCV is usually the first 3 bytes (6 chars), but your example uses 4 bytes (8 chars)
        System.out.println(&quot;Full Cipher: &quot; + resultHex);
        System.out.println(&quot;KCV (4 bytes): &quot; + resultHex.substring(0, 8));
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Full Cipher: 5B4C8BED1635338D KCV (4 bytes): 5B4C8BED</p>
<p>This matches your expected result 5B4C8BED.</p>
<p>For quick verification without writing code, I created an online tool that supports DES/3DES KCV calculation which you can use to cross-check your values:<br />
<strong><a href="https://www.google.com/url?sa=E&amp;q=https%3A%2F%2Fhsmkit.com%2Fkcv-calculator" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Online KCV Calculator</a></strong> (Disclaimer: I am the author of this tool).</p>
