Q: Can a TipKit tip be permanently dismissed / marked as displayed by tapping outside the tip? A: <p>A <code>Tip</code> is permanently dismissed / marked as displayed by calling <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/tipkit/tip/invalidate(reason:)" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>invalidate(reason:)</code></a>.</p>
<p>When the default tip view style is used, the tip is automatically invalidated when the close button is tapped, but not when tapping outside the tip.</p>
<p>However, tips can be configured with a maximum display count, see <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/tipkit/tip/maxdisplaycount" rel="nofollow noreferrer">MaxDisplayCount</a>.</p>
<p>The documentation says:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Use this option to automatically invalidate a tip after it has appeared a specified number of times.</p>
<p>By default tips have no maximum display count.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So, based on what you wrote in the question:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Is there any way to use tap outside to prevent tips from showing multiple times?</p>
<p>Tips should be as least anoying as possible. Thus a simple tap outside should be enough to stop them from showing again.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>...the simplest solution might be to set <code>MaxDisplayCount</code> to 1. This way, once it has been shown, it is automatically invalidated and not shown again, regardless of how it was dismissed.</p>
<p>Normally, this is just a matter of implementing <code>options</code> as a computed property in your <code>Tip</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>struct MyTip: Tip {

    // ... other Tip properties

    var options: [any Option] {
        MaxDisplayCount(1)
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>In your case, you are handling iOS version availability with wrapper constructions, so you will need to include an availability check too (otherwise it doesn't compile):</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>struct SampleTip: Tip, TipSupport {

    // ... other Tip properties

    @available(iOS 17.0, *)
    var options: [any Option] {
        MaxDisplayCount(1)
    }
}
</code></pre>

